    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d163">

                <pb facs="0292" n="202" xml:id="pg202"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">422.11G93/1131: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hartman</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-11-01T14:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 1,
                                1920—2 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>39. No report has been received from you since your 67 September 8, 11
                        a.m.,<anchor n="27" xml:id="d163-f1"/> regarding daily deposits. Department
                    informed by railway company that it fears deposits on hand may be withdrawn if
                    remittances to London not promptly made. Report by cable on daily deposits and
                    what, if any, remittances to London on account of railway bonds have been made.
                    Report also your recommendations with reference to what representations, if any,
                    should be made to Ecuadorean Government in the premises.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
